  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Plan of Approach for sustainable management of the Queule River mouth, Chile</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This assignment aims to provide a Plan of Approach to the Directorate of Port Works of the Chilean government (Direcci&#xF3;n de Obras Portuarias; DOP) for sustainable management of the Queule River mouth. Sustainable, in this context, refers to beneficial to the wetland system, biodiversity and local fisherman.The Plan of Approach is ought to provide insight in the root causes of the sedimentation problems in the estuary, based on available background information. Based on the systems analysis, the plan of approach provide insight in potential nature-based solutions (NBS) benchmark solutions (successfully applied elsewhere), which could fit the context of Queule. Based on stakeholder interaction, a conceptual design is delivered which can be further and explored by DOP in close consultation with local stakeholders.</narrative>
  </description>
